{
  "_comment": "S14d part 2 lesson scenario - The Table (the Peace of Pressburg), December 1805 (docs/TABLE_LESSON_SPEC.md §4). Authored-deterministic like the Danube: no variance bands, no navies, no agendas, no marshal_pool, no moments, no designs, no coalition block, no formables. ONE France-led war on Austria and Russia (Bavaria and the Kingdom of Italy carried in by their own entries), Vienna, the Tyrol and Moravia in French hands, the record's wins on the ledger with France's losses at the record's 9,000 (the table's own-losses term reads the terms and the map, never the ledger; the ledger reaches the table only through the war score, whose blood component nets the dead), Austria exhausted and ready to sign alone, Russia unbeaten at home and not. Bavaria an ally reassured by a mission and made a vassal by the terms Talleyrand suggests, eased once. Every court off the lesson holds its letters until turn 7 (ai_proposal_cooldowns) so the Cabinet is open on the second morning. Its diplomacy is LIVE by design - the verdicts the lesson teaches are the AI's own; jealousy, dotation, petitions and the autosave sleep (tutorial_state.is_school_world). Tuned by tools/_table_board_probe.py.",
